course: dictionary
lesson: 7476
title: Portly: a gentle word for a round body
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Portly» describes a person, usually an older man, who is rather fat and has a large round body. In a story, the clues help: «a cheerful older gentleman» is a kind picture, and portly paints it gently.
explain: Portly is a polite, old-fashioned word. People today often say stout or heavy instead, but you will find portly in old books and in stories about mayors and gentlemen.
explain: Be careful in real life. Calling someone fat, even with a gentler word, is a comment on their body and can hurt. Use words about people kindly, and only when they really matter.
explain: Capital letters are clues too. In «young Portly hasn't learnt to swim very well yet», the capital P and the word «young» show that Portly is a name, not a description. Check the sentence: does «portly» fit before a person, or is it a name?
fact: Portly is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in a portly man.
fact: «Portly» means rather fat, with a large round body.
fact: «Portly» is a polite or old-fashioned word.
fact: «Portly» is often used for older men, and in stories for cheerful characters or mayors.
fact: A capital P can mean a name, as in «young Portly» in the story.
exercise: «The portly gentleman tipped his hat and smiled.» What is portly describing? | The sky, which was grey | *The gentleman, meaning his large round body | The hat, which was tall and black | The river, which was fast
exercise: Which word is a name for a character, not a describing word? «Young Portly hasn't learnt to swim very well yet.» | swim | very | *Portly | Young
exercise: Sam says portly is always a rude word. What is the best answer? | *Portly is polite and old-fashioned, but any comment on someone's body can still hurt | Portly means happy, so it is always kind | Portly means very tiny | Portly is a type of boat
test: Which word means rather fat, with a large round body? | Narrow | Slim | *Portly | Swift
test: In which kind of writing do you most often meet portly? | Texting | *Old-fashioned or story writing | Road signs | Scientific reports
exam: In «Portly wakes with a squeak of joy, then searches the island», what is Portly? | A place on the island | A verb meaning to search | An adjective describing a person | *A name for a character
